            <description><![CDATA[<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:12px}h1,h2{font-size:15px}</style><h2>Kaiju 1.0</h2>
<p>The first release of Kaiju: thanks to everyone who tested the betas.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Files in the cloud</b> (iCloud Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive, Google Drive) that aren't on your Mac yet are downloaded before Kaiju reads them. If one doesn't arrive, Kaiju tells you instead of waiting forever.
</li>
<li><b>Cancel</b> while a file opens. If it takes longer than usual, Kaiju says why it might be.
</li>
<li><b>Hold ⇧ Shift when Kaiju starts</b> to open it without reopening your files.
</li>
<li><b>Sample Builder: loops and phrases on the same note</b> (they all read as C3) now go one per key, in file-name order, instead of overlapping.
</li>
<li><b>Sample Builder: Correct tuning</b> can be turned off. When it's on, a detected note sets the Tune that puts the sample in tune (the audio isn't changed).
</li></ul>]]></description>
